Thanks again for getting the first version of the Consulo Global website together.

I’ve had a good opportunity to go through the site in detail and, overall, and if im being honest Ive been blown away by your work, its super impressive and more importantly Its heading in the right direction. I think you’ve understood what I’m trying to achieve – particularly the specialist industrial positioning, clean design, international reach and distinction between the client and candidate journeys.

Rather than changing the overall concept, I think we now need to refine it and push the design another level. There are also a couple of additions I’d kindly like you to make while we’re still at this stage of the build.

Specialist Markets – adding Electrification & Energy Technologies
I’d like to add a seventh specialist market:

ELECTRIFICATION & ENERGY TECHNOLOGIES

This is an increasingly important area of industrial technology and fits very naturally alongside our existing Automation & Motion Control and Mechanical Power Transmission specialisms.

I’d like this sector to cover areas such as:

Industrial Electrification • Electric Motors • High-Efficiency Motors • Electric Drivetrains • Power Electronics • Inverters • Power Conversion • Energy Storage • Battery Systems • Charging Infrastructure • Electrified Industrial Equipment • Energy Efficiency

There will naturally be some crossover with Automation & Motion Control and Mechanical Power Transmission, but I actually think that helps demonstrate how interconnected these markets are.

I would therefore suggest our seven specialist markets become:

Automation & Motion Control
Mechanical Power Transmission
Electrification & Energy Technologies
Bulk & Material Handling
Industrial Distribution & MRO
Process, Flow & Instrumentation
Combustion & Thermal Technologies

I’ve deliberately changed the existing “Combustion, Thermal & Energy” category to “Combustion & Thermal Technologies” so we’re not using “Energy” across two separate categories.

It could also be interesting visually to communicate the relationship between:

Automation & Motion Control ↔️ Electrification & Energy Technologies ↔️ Mechanical Power Transmission

rather than treating every market as existing completely independently.

Client Experience / Logos
I’d really like to strengthen the client credibility element of the website.

Rather than simply displaying company names, I’d like us to use the actual company logos, subject to the appropriate permissions, and present this section as:

SELECTED CLIENT EXPERIENCE

Companies we have recruited for across industrial technology.

Please also add Pilz and Zimmer Group to the list, so the client experience section would now include:

WEG
Rossi
Brown GearTech
Tsubakimoto
Regina
John King Chain
THK
IKO Nippon
Habasit
Forbo Movement Systems
Pilz
Zimmer Group

Rather than displaying these randomly, I’d like them grouped by their relevant technology ecosystems. There will be some crossover, which is absolutely fine.

For example:

Power Transmission & Drive Technology
WEG • Rossi • Brown GearTech • Tsubakimoto • Regina • John King Chain

Linear Motion, Bearings & Mechatronics
THK • IKO Nippon • Zimmer Group

Automation, Safety & Motion Control
Pilz • Zimmer Group • WEG

Belting & Conveyor Technology
Habasit • Forbo Movement Systems • Regina • Tsubakimoto • John King Chain

I’d also like a smaller selection of the strongest/most recognisable logos displayed on the homepage as an immediate credibility piece, linking through to the fuller Client Experience section.

Individual Specialist Market Pages
I like the direction of the individual market pages, but I think these need slightly more depth and visual interest.

One idea I particularly like is adding a visual “How We Map This Market” section to each page.

For example, Automation & Motion Control could demonstrate:

Direct Technology
Servo Drives → Servo Motors → PLC/HMI → Variable Speed Drives → Motion Control

↓

Adjacent Technology
Robotics → Machine Safety → Sensors → Linear Motion → Mechatronics

↓

Target Organisations
Automation OEMs → Machine Builders → System Integrators → Specialist Distributors

↓

Target Talent
Technical Sales → Applications → Business Development → Product Management → Sales Leadership

We can create equivalent maps for all seven specialist markets.

This would visually demonstrate that Consulo understands how talent moves between technologies, competitors and adjacent markets rather than simply searching by job title.

4. About / Company Positioning

I’d like to make one adjustment to the About page.

I don’t want any individual Director or Founder photography on the website. I want Consulo Global to have a strong corporate identity in its own right and for the visual emphasis to remain on the business, the markets we operate within and the industrial technologies we support.

The objective is to build Consulo Global as an international specialist search brand rather than a personality-led recruitment consultancy.

The About page should therefore focus on:

– The evolution from Consulo First into Consulo Global
– Our specialist industrial heritage and market knowledge
– Our search philosophy and methodology
– The technologies and industries we understand
– Our international reach across the United States, United Kingdom, Continental Europe and Middle East
– Our ambition to continue developing Consulo as a genuinely global industrial technology search business

Visually, rather than individual photography, I’d prefer strong industrial imagery, technology-led graphics, market maps and international/geographical elements that reinforce the scale and positioning of Consulo Global.

The people behind the business can obviously still be found and connected with through LinkedIn, but I don’t want individual profiles to become part of the main visual identity of the website.

 

Search Stories
I’d like to add a Search Stories section, ideally sitting underneath Clients rather than adding another item to the main navigation.

These would be short, anonymised case studies showing the thinking behind selected searches.

Examples could include:

– Building a regional technical sales team for a global linear motion manufacturer
– Identifying commercial talent beyond the obvious gearbox candidate pool
– Finding a commercial leader within a specialist chain/material handling ecosystem
– Building commercial capability within a new international territory

Each Search Story could follow:

The Business → The Challenge → What Made the Search Difficult → How We Mapped the Market → Search Strategy → Outcome

The objective isn’t to reveal confidential client or candidate information. It’s to demonstrate how Consulo actually approaches specialist industrial searches.

Overall Visual Development
I really like the clean direction of the site and don’t want to fundamentally change it.

However, as we move from the rough concept towards the finished design, I’d like us to push the visual treatment another level and make the site feel more like a premium international industrial search consultancy.

In particular:

– More high-quality, authentic industrial imagery
– Actual client logos rather than text representations
– Stronger use of the charcoal/yellow Consulo palette
– Visual market-mapping diagrams
– More breathing space between major sections
– Subtle animation and hover interactions
– Greater visual differentiation between the seven specialist markets
– Avoiding too much repetition of the same card/text layouts as visitors move through the site

I don’t want the site to become flashy or over-designed. It should remain clean, technical, modern and professional.

Insights
I really like the positioning of this as “Industrial Recruitment & Market Intelligence” rather than simply calling it a blog, so let’s retain that.

For launch, however, I’d prefer to have three strong articles live initially and then progressively publish the others. This gives us an ongoing stream of website and LinkedIn content following launch rather than making the Insights section look artificially populated from day one.

Overall, I’m very happy with the foundations. The homepage proposition, search methodology, international positioning and specialist-market approach are all heading exactly where I want them.

The next stage for me is about adding more proof, personality and visual sophistication – together with bringing Electrification & Energy Technologies properly into the Consulo proposition.

Have a look at the above and let me know your thoughts. I’m very happy for you to bring your own creative ideas to these areas as well. I want the final site to combine the market/content direction I’ve provided with your design and development expertise.
